[case note by Katie Hoban on 2026-10-16 "Onboarding - Pension Transfer"]
Initial meeting held with Abby on 16/10.&nbsp;
Meeting focused on improving her family’s financial position following her move to Netflix and increased earnings. Her primary objective is to clear their £60,000&nbsp;credit card debt. The agreed strategy is to use her higher income and upcoming bonuses to aggressively reduce the balances before transferring any remaining debt to a 0% interest credit card. Debt repayment was identified as the immediate priority ahead of building savings or making additional investments.&nbsp;
Katie recommended that Abby contribute 7% to Netflix’s workplace pension through salary sacrifice to secure the maximum employer contribution and benefit from tax efficiencies. Existing pension arrangements, including a private pension valued at approximately £120,000, will be reviewed and details gathered for potential consolidation.&nbsp;
The meeting also considered the impact of Abby’s income exceeding £100,000, including the effect on personal allowance and childcare support. While tax planning opportunities were discussed, debt reduction remains the priority. Abby decided not to participate in Netflix stock options at this stage due to concentration risk and her preference to focus on reducing debt.&nbsp;
Looking ahead, Abby’s next goals are to build emergency savings, review existing protection arrangements, and begin saving towards her children's future private school fees. Katie will gather pension information, review protection policies, and prepare a cash flow model ahead of the next meeting.&nbsp;
LOAs sent along with factfind link. Next meeting will be to present cashflow.&nbsp;

