[task note by Jim Hoban on 2026-03-19 "Client Feedback & Instructions"]
From: Chris Fleming &lt;chris.j.fleming@btinternet.com&gt; 
Sent: 15 March 2026 19:44
To: Jim Hoban &lt;jim@hobanfp.com&gt;
Cc: Tommie Hoban &lt;tommie@hobanfp.com&gt;; 'Paul Colman' &lt;paul.colman@gunnercooke.com&gt;; liz.a.fleming@btinternet.com
Subject: RE: Your Estate Planning Strategy - Executive Summary
Hi Jim,
Apologies for the delay in getting back to you.

 Yes,      we’re happy with the overall approach and would like to proceed;
 We’d      initially like to invest approximately £1 million;
 We’d      like to proceed with all of the Trust structures;
 We’d      like to go ahead with the Whole of Life cover.  Not sure that we need      the GIVIOS policies as well, albeit the premiums are relatively      insignificant;
 We are      comfortable with the fees.

A couple of questions that I had:

 In your previous email you mentioned that “We also      discussed the potential benefit of introducing debt against your £1.5      million property to both reduce your taxable estate and provide capital      for the FIC.”  How does this reduce the taxable      estate?  If we borrowed, say, £1 million and lent it to the FIC then      the value of our estate would be unchanged wouldn’t it?  There would      just be an additional loan in and a loan out?
 Just to      confirm – the two CGT hold over trusts are completely separate from the      FIC aren’t they?

Regards,
Chris

